<title>ITALY: Bologna air cargo traffic up 30.6pct, Pisa up 4.6.</title>
<headline>Bologna air cargo traffic up 30.6pct, Pisa up 4.6.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic at Bologna's airport rose 30.6 percent in June 1997 to 1,184 tonnes against the same period 1996, managing company SAB said.</p>
<p>Pisa airport, also managed by SAB, handled 338 tonnes of cargo traffic in June 1997, up 4.62 percent.</p>
<p>Details in tonnes included:</p>
<p>			   Jun 97   Pct change     Jan-Jun 97    Pct change</p>
<p>					vs Jun 96			vs Jan-Jun 96</p>
<p>BOLOGNA</p>
<p> Cargo flown		789	up 30.6	   4,789	up 20.8</p>
<p> trucked		    395	up  2.8	   2,217	down 6.1</p>
<p> Total traffic	  1,184	up 19.8	   7,006	up 10.7</p>
<p> Total mail		 223    down  7.3	   1,418	down 2.4</p>
<p> Total passengers   239,374	up 14.0     1,158,000	up 15.1</p>
<p>PISA</p>
<p> Cargo flown		338	up  4.6	   2,155	down 7.6</p>
<p> trucked		    316	up 62.2	   1,805	  up 18.3</p>
<p> Total traffic	    653	up 26.3	   3,960	  up 2.7</p>
<p> Total mail		  72	up 45.6	     452	  up 62.0</p>
<p> Total passengers   100,619	up  9.0	 485,082	down 4.3</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
